define('text!live-sql/components/change-log/CHANGELOG.md',[],function () { return '### Version 26.4.1 – April 30, 2026\n\n#### Changed\n- **Splitter and panel behavior**: Allow splitter to collapse completely.\n\n---\n\n### Version 26.4.0 – April 29, 2026\n\n#### Added\n- **Dark mode**: Added a dark theme across the Worksheet, SQL Tutorials, content pages, Object Navigator, and other major application surfaces.\n- **Expanded Object Browser workflows**: Added in-app creation for supported database objects and expanded editing support directly from the Object Browser, enabling users to modify definitions and properties of supported database objects directly within the interface.\n\n#### Changed\n- **SQL Tutorials experience**: Renamed the Library experience to SQL Tutorials and improved navigation, filtering, and content browsing throughout the app.\n- **Splitter and panel behavior**: Upgraded splitter behavior for smoother resizing and improved responsive panel interactions across the application.\n\n#### Fixed\n- **Object Browser and editor reliability**: Fixed several issues affecting object editing flows, busy-state handling, and object-specific interactions in the browser.\n- **Worksheet and Quick SQL reliability**: Fixed issues around worksheet storage, opening files, loading states, and panel behavior to improve day-to-day editing reliability.\n\n---\n\n### Version 26.1.2 – January 16, 2026\n\n#### Fixed\n- Fixed issues when using timezones such as GMT+5:30\n\n---\n\n### Version 26.1.1 – January 15, 2026\n\n#### Added\n- Enable drag-and-drop of column names from object navigator\n\n---\n\n### Version 26.1.0 – January 7, 2026\n\n#### Added\n- **Object Browser Slider**: Introduced a new slider interface in the FreeSQL Object Browser, allowing users to quickly view detailed information about database objects from within the same panel.\n- **DBMS_XPLAN FORMAT support**: The custom dbms_xplan now accepts the FORMAT parameter ("BASIC", "TYPICAL", "ALL") for flexible plan output.\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.11.0 – November 19, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Added a new **“Create a SQL Developer for VS Code connection”** option in the **“Connect with…”** panel to quickly open **SQL Developer for VS Code** and start a new connection setup\n- **JavaScript language support** in the “Share Code” language dropdown list.\n- **Quick SQL syntax highlighting** in the Worksheet. The parser now recognizes Quick SQL and applies the appropriate styles.\n\n### Changed\n- **Dirty worksheet handling** now uses *Save and Close* dialogs instead of the previous *Change Mode* dialog.\n\n### Fixed\n- **Quick SQL settings not applied** when generating DDL, including:\n  - *On Delete* policy not affecting generated DDL.\n  - *Add PK* option causing broken DDL generation when relations are present.\n  - General Quick SQL configuration inconsistencies in the output.\n- **Unable to log JavaScript statements** in SQL History.\n- **Missing cancel/close button** in the “Generate New Password” panel for schema connections.\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.10.0 – October 8, 2025\n\n#### Added\n- **SQLNet** Added Schema Access and Connections Details (SQLNet) feature to allow users to access their Live SQL schema externally\n- Added Wrapper for DBMS_XPLAN (MY_USER_XPLAN) for User-Specific Explain Plans\n\n#### Fixed\n\n- Fixed Script statements actions menu changing position in Safari browser\n- Fixed Database version labels to maintain consistent over all the application\n- Fixed clipboard notification misplaced when clicking in DBMS Output\n- Fixed limitation that restricted the number of statements in scripts and tutorials to 26\n- Fixed title for Upload Script slider\n- Fixed issue where Setup Code Text Tools lack visual feedback when activated or deactivated\n- Fixed issue where users couldn\'t format content when creating tutorials or scripts\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.8.1 – August 12, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Added **404 - Not Found** page\n- Error handling when restoring the last used database version\n- QuickSQL - split the code editor in two sections: one for writing code and another for displaying results in real time\n\n#### Changed\n\n- Improved number formatting to Likes and Executions\n\n#### Fixed\n\n- Fixed issue when multiple library filters requests were triggered in quick succession\n- Fixed issue with Share Dialog not closing when trying to unshare resource\n- Fixed issue where signing out left no tab selection in Library\n- Fix broken footer not displaying items correctly\n- Fix sorting for migrated SQL History statements\n- Fixed issue where authenticated users were left with read-only access after resuming a session following more than 1 hour of inactivity\n- Fixed issue where cancelling the Delete Tutorial/Script Dialog would not keep the user to the resource page\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.8.0 – August 8, 2025\n\n#### Changed\n\n- Improve SQL parser performance for faster query processing\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.7.0 – July 2, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Support for **MLE/JavaScript** code execution\n- Clickable version info + Changelog dialog: You can now click the version number at the bottom-right of the app to view the full changelog\n\n#### Changed\n\n- Improve schema naming in Object Navigator for better clarity\n\n#### Fixed\n\n- Fixed issue where file upload failed during script creation, preventing statement insertion\n- Fix issue with auto-complete not showing table list for schema in SQL Worksheet\n- Fix statement details result not showing for read-only users\n- Fix filter labels for database versions\n- Fixed `NEXTVAL` sequence error when selecting from newly created sequences in SQL\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.6.1 – June 10, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- New feature **Run in FreeSQL**. You can now add a "Run in FreeSQL" button to blogs or docs. It opens the code in a new tab with FreeSQL Worksheet preloaded, making it easy for readers to try examples instantly.\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.6.0 – June 3, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Add database version filter support for **19c** and **23ai**\n- Apply filters to scripts depending on selected schema version\n- Support **multiple DB versions** with user-selectable schema\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.4.1 – April 15, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Improve library navigation: redirect users to last active tab\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.4.0 – April 3, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Add support for **Quick SQL**\n- Create **temporary home page** with redirect buttons for FreeSQL and Live SQL Classic\n- Implement **Save as Script** functionality from SQL history\n- Add **Help and Feedback** button in header\n- Add SQL+ style mode in **Script Output** (SQL followed by result)\n- Extend Library search to work in the Worksheet Library\n\n#### Changed\n\n- Enable logging of executed SQL*Plus statements in SQL history\n\n#### Fixed\n\n- Fix encoding issue by encoding characters in UTF-8\n- Fix issue where upload script button creates content without selecting a file\n- Fix incorrect error labels in code editor for unexpected symbols\n- Fix library filters for parent-child selection issues\n- Fix: unable to delete tutorial prerequisite when editing an empty field\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.1.1 – January 17, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Suggest schema names when object does not exist in current schema\n- Add error messages to script output\n- Add LiveSQL external code support through query parameter\n- Add warning banner under worksheet toolbar when dealing with external code\n\n#### Removed\n\n- Stop saving comments in SQL history\n- Remove autocomplete from delete account dialog\n\n#### Fixed\n\n- Fix keyboard shortcuts for **Format** and **Clear**\n- Fix issue where **Query Result** and **Script Output** have different date format\n- Fix issue where Read-only code blocks in tutorials/scripts can be typed in\n\n---\n\n### Version 25.1.0 – January 03, 2025\n\n#### Added\n\n- Grant `DBMS_DATA_MINING` privileges to users for data mining support\n- Display release version in footer\n\n#### Removed\n\n- Disable opposite-direction swipe from closing slider in tutorial steps\n\n#### Changed\n\n- Always display **HR** sample schema in Object Navigator when the tour is triggered\n\n---\n\n### Version beta2 – December 14, 2024\n\n#### Added\n\n- Incorporate a **Return to Live SQL Classic** button into the header\n- Implement **drag-and-drop** within the Object Navigator\n- Grant `CREATE PROPERTY GRAPH` privilege to schemas\n- Add missing tooltips throughout the app\n\n#### Fixed\n\n- Fix: Query result error wasn\'t showing completely due to scroll issue\n- Fix: upload script was failing to import statements if the title is empty\n- Fix: Public scripts were not appearing in community search results\n\n#### Changed\n\n- Show display name instead of email in Library\n- Enhance Library page to support query parameter for search functionality\n- Improve LiveSQL Tour Flow: Move SQL execution instruction to Step 2\n- Load additional sample schemas into the application\n\n---\n\n### Version beta1 – November 18, 2024\n\nLaunch Day\n';});

